@@ -0,0 +1,47 @@
+# B01 upstream configuration and startup
+
+B01 establishes the task/metric contract and configures existing benchmark assets.
+For a theory-only claim, retain the supported formal contract alternative; do not
+require a dataset, executable evaluator or GPU startup for formal-only work.
+Prefer the benchmark authors' implementation and documented settings. Pin the
+published repository/package revision, dataset configuration/split, dependency
+versions, data/model paths, selected interpreter and actual invocation. Reuse
+already supplied SSH authority and confirmed resources. Define the GPU and execution
+environment at intake and reuse that target throughout the run; machine migration
+is not part of the normal B01 flow. Revisit the target only on an explicit user
+change or an observed loss of access.
+
+Perform one real import/configuration/entrypoint startup check on the authorized
+execution server. Read its exit code and retained output. Fix an actual dependency
+or invocation error if observed. Once these checks pass, submit B01 setup evidence
+for independent acceptance and continue the prescribed sequence. Do not request
+repeated literature searches, custom correctness proofs or fabricated incorrect
+samples just to configure a published tool. Recheck only changed components or
+an actual new failure.
+
+Preserve the original task population, setup code, prompts, metric and denominator.
+An upstream package being installed does not authorize replacing MBPP full/test
+with MBPP+ or a sanitized subset. Record such differences. If authors provide
+data and evaluation instructions but no executable scorer, state that fact and
+name the actual community/project executor honestly; never relabel it official.
+Lack of an author-provided executable is an outstanding scoring integration fact,
+not a reason to repeat B01 indefinitely after its configuration work is complete.
+
+Startup success proves only configuration/startup. Baseline runs, scorer behavior,
+adaptation/parity checks and generated-program isolation belong to B03/the actual
+scoring stage. Retain those obligations and unscored outputs. No automatic
+scientific PASS, threshold changes, test removal or native-admission exemption
+follows from B01 acceptance.
+
+For an existing pinned Work Harness, the owner can adopt a scoped B01 setup policy
+with `ResearchProgram.adopt_b01_setup(project_id, policy_ref,
+expected_revision=...)` at a quiet B01 decision boundary. The policy pins the user
+instruction, exact execution target and observed setup report. Runtime supplies
+the same effective criteria to both worker and reviewer and records the policy
+with acceptance; historical catalog and accepted-step pins stay intact.
+
+For setup-only acceptance (`tasks=[]`), retain the exact accepted scientific
+decision reference instead of inventing a new inquiry/frame merely to acknowledge
+an import. Fresh native scientific receipts or new child work retain their normal
+decision and review requirements. Existing coverage and future scoring obligations
+cannot be erased. The setup report identifies pending scoring explicitly.
